WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.434 --> 00:00:04.080
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.660
- [Justine] Right now,
we are at Kualoa Ranch

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.730
and this is probably one
of my most favorite places,

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.100
I think, in the entire world.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.880
It is the most beautiful ranch.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.250
There's over 4,000 acres

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.100
and they have shot so many films here.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.140
I'm pretty sure you guys
have seen so many of them.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.850
We also did a really amazing
tour here back in October.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.130
I never posted that vlog,

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.350
but today you're finally
gonna get to see it.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.370
But first, we're gonna hop on this boat

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.220
and go to small, tiny cool island.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.320
I have a lot of stuff!

00:00:28.345 --> 00:00:31.845
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.670
So guys, one thing that
I definitely recommend

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.980
you should never drone from a moving boat.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.480
It's a really bad idea.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.840
So thankfully, we're not moving.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.360
I mean, it's definitely possible,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.810
but I would not recommend it.

00:00:50.687 --> 00:00:54.187
(upbeat electronic music)

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.780
So I'm about to attempt
a really fun drone shot.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.270
I basically want to fly it
through this little boat

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.900
and up and away, so
let's hope that it works.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:31.733
I'm gonna try two,

00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:34.455
I'm gonna do one facing me
and then one facing away.

00:01:34.455 --> 00:01:36.089
Fingers crossed, guys.

00:01:36.089 --> 00:01:38.589
(drone whirs)

00:01:40.336 --> 00:01:42.003
It looks so awesome!

00:01:43.888 --> 00:01:47.388
(upbeat electronic music)

00:02:14.776 --> 00:02:18.276
(bright electronic music)

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.460
They filmed Jurassic Park here!

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.410
They filmed so many movies,
and we're going to go

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.020
to all those locations and check them out.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.300
So let's go, we've got
to go rally the troops.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.360
We are here with our
family and our friend Susie

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.401
and I don't know where
Bree went, she's somewhere.

00:02:57.401 --> 00:03:00.901
(bright electronic music)

00:03:04.102 --> 00:03:05.309
- [Man] Alright, so he's
gonna be your tour guide.

00:03:05.309 --> 00:03:06.442
- [Women] Hi.

00:03:06.442 --> 00:03:07.723
- [Justine] I'm Justine, nice to meet you!

00:03:07.723 --> 00:03:08.570
- [Tour Guide] Nice to meet you!

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:11.270
- [Justine] Alright,
everybody hop in! Get in!

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.687
(group yells excitedly)

00:03:12.687 --> 00:03:13.904
- Can I sit in the front?

00:03:13.904 --> 00:03:15.005
- [Tour Guide] You can.

00:03:15.005 --> 00:03:16.005
- Okay! Yes!

00:03:18.077 --> 00:03:19.643
Everyone have enough room?

00:03:19.643 --> 00:03:20.630
- [Woman] Have everybody?

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.683
(everybody cheers)

00:03:22.683 --> 00:03:25.023
Hello, wow! This is great!

00:03:25.023 --> 00:03:28.106
(bright funky music)

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.060
So this is where Jurassic
World was filmed,

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.610
and the helicopter that
took off in the beginning

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.140
was actually right here,
but they dismantled it

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.350
because they didn't
want actual helicopters

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:56.230
to land here inside of the ranch.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.510
The visitor's center was
brought in all by CGI,

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:01.110
so basically, this was a
canvas for them to start with.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.460
And, the rest of it was
all filled in with CGI.

00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:08.077
(bright funky music)

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.180
This is probably my favorite
part so far of the tour.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.400
This is where the T-Rex
escaped at the beginning

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.233
of the movie.

00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:22.120
And they said that normally on movie sets

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.910
they end up taking down all of the props

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.290
and things like that, but this

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.810
they left up because it was
a very highly requested thing

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.890
that people wanted to see on the tour.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:31.140
This is so cool!

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:32.310
This is the lookout behind us.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.780
We're gonna go up there
right now, but they said that

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.320
they're doing some
construction on the glass.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.740
Because, all of this stuff
had to sort of be remade.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.870
Because, originally, when
things are created for movies,

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:42.230
they're all tore down because
they're not built to last.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:45.460
Especially, in Hawaii in
tropical conditions like this.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:46.530
We're goin' up, look here it is!

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.430
Ah, this is so cool!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.847
I'm freaking out guys, I'm so excited.

00:04:51.607 --> 00:04:52.774
Look the iPad!

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.550
Not sure which gen this is?

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:57.890
Hmm, I don't think
they've updated to iOS 11.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:01.321
And the Photo Booth app,
somebody definitely Googled

00:05:01.321 --> 00:05:02.407
(laughs) iPad screen.

00:05:02.407 --> 00:05:06.237
Next stop.

00:05:06.237 --> 00:05:09.404
(slow ethereal music)

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:35.831
(moving electronic music)

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.430
Behind me is the restaurant
where they filmed

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:49.700
for 50 First Dates with Adam
Sandler and Drew Barrymore.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.030
I've got some popcorn here.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.850
It's snack time and break on the tour.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.740
But, this is so pretty.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:55.990
Like, isn't this awesome?

00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:58.820
- So this right here is where

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.707
they docked the submarine in Lost.

00:06:00.707 --> 00:06:01.540
- [Justine] Wow.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.207
- [Man] Did you know that, John?

00:06:10.723 --> 00:06:13.640
(Tour Guide sings)

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.153
- [Justine] This is such an awesome view!

00:06:21.166 --> 00:06:24.666
(upbeat electronic music)

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:41.880
Right here is Hurley's
golf course from Lost,

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.710
if you guys remember that from the show.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.023
Any Lost fans? God I love that show.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.773
Those right there are
Godzilla's footsteps.

00:06:55.773 --> 00:06:57.410
They're pretty huge.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:58.680
Now that I'm up close to it,

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.860
it just kind looks like a big dirt hole.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.710
You would never be able to
tell that this was a footstep.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:09.353
Well, this is a pretty cool view.

00:07:10.455 --> 00:07:13.205
(cheerful music)

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.560
This is from Kong: Skull Island,

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.770
I never saw the movie,
so I'm not really sure

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:29.870
what this is in reference to,

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.600
but now I'm gonna have to see it,

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:34.873
and then I'll be able to
be like wow, we were there.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.920
(Justine laughs)

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:41.783
There should be a shrine nearby!

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:09.340
We're now heading into
the World War II bunkers,

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.983
which is also doubled
as some scenes for Lost.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:18.603
(muffled chatter)

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.080
Hey! Awh here it is, the Lost, this is

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.583
what I was looking for! Yes!

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:32.312
This is unbelieva-
(group screams)

00:08:32.312 --> 00:08:33.645
Awh, I hate you!

00:08:37.246 --> 00:08:38.402
- [Man] Did we actually get you?

00:08:38.402 --> 00:08:40.370
- You actually did, oh my god

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.743
I was really scared I'm crying!

00:08:42.743 --> 00:08:44.120
- That was a genuine yell.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.303
- [Justine] I was freaking scared,

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.030
oh my god, I hate you.

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:51.480
Anyway, now that I am not

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.463
as terrified as I was before.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:57.590
- [Jenna] You yelled so loud.

00:08:58.605 --> 00:09:01.938
(slow electronic music)

00:09:18.392 --> 00:09:20.380
Guys, thank you so much
for watching this vlog,

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.180
that was basically, it seems like almost,

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:23.750
six months in the making.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.120
I love this place, and if
you guys are ever in Oahu,

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.990
I definitely recommend,
you have to check it out

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.270
because it is just
incredibly breathtaking.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:33.060
The views, the scenery,
and all of the people here

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:35.380
are so nice that it's such an experience,

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.960
and I hope that one day you
guys can also experience it too,

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.470
but now, that's it, that's
the end of the vlog!

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:41.670
I'll see you guys later.

